WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.500
Every January, Dimas writes the same line and sticks it on his wall: this year, I will get better at data analysis.

2
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:19.200
By March, the note is still there. Nothing else has changed.

3
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.500
The problem is not his effort. It is the sentence.

4
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:29.800
“Better” is an adjective. It gives him nothing to check.

5
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.100
So he crosses it out.

6
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:42.100
The new sentence has a result he can count, and a date: by 30 June, three finished projects, shown to a mentor.

7
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:49.000
Next, time. His first plan is two hours every day. It survives nine days.

8
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:57.900
His second plan is smaller: three sessions of forty minutes, booked in his calendar like classes he cannot skip.

9
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:03.600
A modest plan you keep beats an ambitious one you imagine.

10
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:10.500
Last, a signal. Every Sunday evening, Dimas checks one number: sessions kept this week.

11
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:18.200
Three of three, carry on. One of three, make the plan smaller, not the guilt bigger.

12
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.700
Put together, a working intention has four parts.

13
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.000
A result you can count.

14
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
A date.

15
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.100
A weekly time budget you can defend.

16
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.200
And one signal you check every Sunday.

17
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.100
Intentions with a number and a date get finished.

18
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:45.400
Intentions with adjectives get abandoned.

19
00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:48.700
Defend a modest time budget.

20
00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.200
Measure progress every week, or it quietly stops.

21
00:01:53.200 --> 00:02:02.200
Now it is your turn. Write your one sentence for The Map: a result, a date, a weekly budget and a Sunday signal.
